      "id": "stageshow",
      "repo": "benjitaylor/skills",
      "commit": "802057409787133703c56001080169e347305572",
      "license": "MIT (code)",
      "author": "Benji Taylor",
      "goesInto": "motion",
      "into": "skills/motion/references/vendor/stageshow",
      "take": [
        {
          "from": "stageshow",
          "to": "stageshow",
          "skill": true
        }
      ],
      "exclude": [
        "stageshow/assets/app-icons.ts",
        "stageshow/kit/brands/**",
        "stageshow/package-lock.json",
        "stageshow/package.json",
        "stageshow/playground/**",
        "stageshow/teaching/**",
        "stageshow/scripts/**",
        "stageshow/examples/phones/**",
        "stageshow/examples/bento/**",
        "stageshow/examples/parts/**",
        "stageshow/examples/google-docs/**",
        "stageshow/examples/google-calendar/**",
        "stageshow/examples/kit-extras/**",
        "stageshow/examples/figma/**",
        "stageshow/examples/brand-marks/**",
        "stageshow/examples/gmail/**",
        "stageshow/examples/linear/**",
        "stageshow/examples/excel/**",
        "stageshow/examples/hero-demo/**",
        "stageshow/examples/wikipedia/index.tsx",
        "stageshow/examples/wikipedia/wiki.css",
        "stageshow/examples/finder/**",
        "stageshow/examples/finder-glass/**",
        "stageshow/examples/imessage/**",
        "stageshow/examples/notion/**",
        "stageshow/examples/powerpoint/**",
        "stageshow/examples/raycast/**",
        "stageshow/examples/slack/**",
        "stageshow/examples/spotify/**",
        "stageshow/examples/telegram/**",
        "stageshow/examples/dynamic-island/**",
        "stageshow/examples/wikipedia/**"
      ],
      "licenseFrom": "stageshow",
      "notes": "Third-party artwork is not vendored: `assets/app-icons.ts` and `kit/brands/**` (not MIT, see NOTICE.md), so imports of them in `kit/` and `examples/` do not resolve. Also not vendored: `package*.json`, `playground/`, `teaching/` and `scripts/` (tooling, not needed to read the skill). Example scenes that embed or import third-party marks are not vendored: phones, bento, parts (import `assets/app-icons.ts`); google-docs, google-calendar, gmail, figma, kit-extras, brand-marks (import `kit/brands` marks of Google, Figma, Slack, Notion, Linear, Gmail and others); linear and excel (replicas of Linear and Microsoft Excel product marks and glyphs); hero-demo (icons copied from a real product toolbar); wikipedia `index.tsx` and `wiki.css` (draw the Wikipedia globe and wordmark). The CC0 photographs and `examples/wikipedia/PHOTOS.md` are kept. `kit/BrandMark` code is kept but its artwork is not, so brand names do not resolve. Also excluded, to keep the public repo clear of real-product replicas: finder, finder-glass, imessage, dynamic-island (Apple), notion, powerpoint, raycast, slack, spotify, telegram. Kept, but not all of it is the author's own artwork: `kit/phone.tsx` glyphs are adapted from Apple's iOS UI kit, `kit/cursors.tsx` has traced macOS cursors and `kit/parts/Icon.tsx` is SF Symbols-style. Check the upstream NOTICE.md before reusing these in a product."
    },
